    "def_lambda_title": "Time Friction Rate (λ) Zone & Implementation Delays",
    "def_lambda_p1": "Models how the passage of time and operational lags dampen or discount the effective strength of direct causal relationships. Strategically, interventions that take 3 to 5 years to materialize face higher friction and risk than immediate actions.",
    "def_lambda_formula_desc": "Where A_ij is nominal influence [-3, 3], t_ij is time delay in years/periods, and λ is the continuous friction discount rate.",
    "def_lambda_box1_title": "Interpretation of λ Values:",
    "def_lambda_box1_li1": "<b>λ = 0.00:</b> Zero time friction. Far-future causal chains retain 100% of their nominal strength.",
    "def_lambda_box1_li2": "<b>λ = 0.10 (Standard Calibration):</b> Realistic moderate discount (a 3-year link retains ~74% impact; a 7-year link retains ~50%).",
    "def_lambda_box1_li3": "<b>λ ≥ 0.30:</b> High friction; prioritizes short-term and immediate direct impacts almost exclusively.",
    "def_lambda_box2_title": "Decision-Making Implication:",
    "def_lambda_box2_p": "Calibrates the prospective model to the institutional planning horizon. When rapid payoffs are vital, a higher λ highlights variables that drive immediate progress despite implementation lags.",
    "def_alpha_title": "Spectral Convergence Factor (α) & Spectral Ratio (α · ρ)",
    "def_alpha_p1": "Replaces Godet's classical powers W^k (which collapse by Perron-Frobenius theorem to an identical dominant eigenvector) with the <b>Katz-Bonacich / Leontief Inverse resolvent operator</b>.",
    "def_alpha_formula_desc": "Infinite geometric sum of all direct, secondary, tertiary, and higher-order indirect paths with strict mathematical attenuation.",
    "def_alpha_box1_title": "Spectral Convergence Condition:",
    "def_alpha_box1_p": "To ensure that the Neumann series converges to a finite and stable mathematical limit, it is strictly required that: <code>α · ρ(|W|) < 1</code>, where ρ(|W|) is the spectral radius (maximal matrix eigenvalue).",
    "def_alpha_box2_title": "Calibration Ratio (Default 0.80):",
    "def_alpha_box2_p": "Sets <code>α = 0.80 / ρ(|W|)</code>. This assigns meaningful weight to 2nd, 3rd, and 4th order causal chains while preventing divergence, keeping each variable's profile distinct.",
    "def_omega_title": "Mean System Ambiguity (Ω̄) & Causal Dissipation",
    "def_omega_p1": "Measures the exact percentage of motricity lost or neutralized due to polarity conflicts: when a variable positively stimulates a target directly, but indirectly dampens it through opposing feedback loops.",
    "def_omega_formula_desc": "Ω_i ranges from 0% (full coherence, zero contradiction) to 100% (total cancellation, zero net impact). Mean Ambiguity Ω̄ is the system-wide average across all variables.",
    "def_omega_box1_title": "Interpretation of Ambiguity Levels:",
    "def_omega_box1_li1": "<b>Ω̄ < 15% (Low):</b> Highly synergistic network. Strategic intent travels cleanly to final outcomes.",
    "def_omega_box1_li2": "<b>15% ≤ Ω̄ ≤ 30% (Moderate):</b> Typical institutional friction and balancing counter-loops.",
    "def_omega_box1_li3": "<b>Ω̄ > 30% (High):</b> Severe structural contradiction. A major portion of leadership efforts and budget dissipates in collateral friction.",
    "def_omega_box2_title": "Diagnostic Value:",
    "def_omega_box2_p": "Explains why seemingly logical policies stall: counteracting feedback loops cancel out gross motricity before reaching destination results.",
    "def_palancas_title": "Consistent Master Levers",
    "def_palancas_p1": "The most reliable, high-yield variables for leadership intervention. They possess tremendous systemic drive combined with an uninhibited causal path free from destructive internal pushback.",
    "def_palancas_formula_desc": "Quantitative criteria: High Net Motricity combined with low ambiguity dissipation from contradictory loops.",
    "def_palancas_box1_title": "Core Characteristics:",
    "def_palancas_box1_li1": "Produce sustained cumulative momentum in the intended direction.",
    "def_palancas_box1_li2": "Do not trigger unintended backlashes that neutralize strategic gains.",
    "def_palancas_box1_li3": "Maximize return on invested budget and organizational political capital.",
    "def_palancas_box2_title": "Policy Recommendation:",
    "def_palancas_box2_p": "Should form the <b>execution core of the strategic plan</b>. Prioritizing resource allocation here yields the most predictable, lasting outcomes.",
    "def_trampas_title": "Policy Traps (Causal Mirages)",
    "def_trampas_p1": "Variables that in classical Godet MICMAC appear as top drivers due to inflated gross motricity, but under signed dynamic analysis prove to be <b>managerial mirages</b>.",
    "def_trampas_formula_desc": "Identification: Apparent high driving power, contradicted by a high internal dissipation rate (high Ω).",
    "def_trampas_box1_title": "Typical Executive Trap:",
    "def_trampas_box1_p": "Pushing these variables in isolation triggers heavy spending and executive frustration: the induced push awakens dormant resistance and regulatory feedback that swallow the gains.",
    "def_trampas_box2_title": "Proper Management Strategy:",
    "def_trampas_box2_p": "<b>Avoid direct, isolated pushes</b>. Prior to intervening, unblock and neutralize balancing resistance loops (e.g., culture shifts, incentive redesign, stakeholder buy-in).",
    "modal_footer_hint": "Tip: Click on any KPI card or control to jump straight to its definition.",
