    "godet_crit_intro": "Michel Godet's method confirms whether the <b>relative priority ranking</b> freezes when chaining indirect effects. Once Spearman reaches <code>ρₛ ≥ 0.98</code>, variables identified as key levers will not change rank through further iterations.",
    "godet_crit_1_t": "1. Confuses rank order with real stability:",
    "godet_crit_1_p": "Five variables can collapse or explode numerically toward infinity while keeping their relative rank order intact (ρₛ = 1.0). Godet does not evaluate whether the real system converges or diverges.",
    "godet_crit_2_t": "2. Ignores polarity signs (+ and −):",
    "godet_crit_2_p": "Godet only sums positive magnitudes. It fails to distinguish between self-regulating negative loops (homeostatic brakes) and destabilizing positive loops (vicious or virtuous cycles).",
    "godet_crit_3_t": "3. Perron-Frobenius Collapse:",
    "godet_crit_3_p": "By multiplying Mᵏ without an attenuation factor, all rows inevitably collapse onto the dominant eigenvector u·vᵀ, erasing the distinct causal signatures of individual variables.",
    "godet_crit_4_t": "4. Timelessness (Lacks physical time):",
    "godet_crit_4_p": "Power k is an abstract algebraic step. It does not model friction, institutional inertia, or the real chronological timeline over which outcomes materialize.",
    "godet_crit_btn": "👉 Explore Advanced Stability (Katz-Bonacich, Triads & Networks)",
